 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "n, e1, t1, e2 and c are positive integers. Choose k with 0 <= k <= n. Energy starts at 0; after the elevator it is k * e1 and the time is k * t1. Then each of the n - k stair floors, in turn, requires the current energy E to be positive, adds ceil(c / E) to the time and lowers E by e2. A choice of k is feasible when the energy is positive before every stair floor. Return the minimum total time over all feasible k.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
